{:edb/db-before-t 647 :edb/db-after-t 648 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533960 50 #inst "2026-10-05T17:41:02.588Z" 13194139533960 true] [17592186068651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186268955 13194139533960 true] [17592186068651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186268962 13194139533960 true] [17592186068652 1020 #edb/ref 17592186268969 13194139533960 true] [17592186068714 1020 #edb/ref 17592186268976 13194139533960 true] [17592186068714 1020 #edb/ref 17592186268983 13194139533960 true] [17592186268955 1017 #edb/ref 17592186268956 13194139533960 true] [17592186268955 1089 "q-113710" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268955 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533960 true] [17592186268955 1100 "Calculate $\\int 2{x}^{5}(4+{x}^{6})^{5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268955 1113 #uuid "4f37db1f-70e6-5494-bcff-bbda79f12583" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268955 1145 "In this case, the term $2{x}^{5}$ outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $4+{x}^{6}.$ But the derivative is $6{x}^{5},$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=4+{x}^{6}.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{5}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=2{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{5}(4+{x}^{6})^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4+{x}^{6})^{5}\\cdot 2{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}(4+{x}^{6})^{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(4+{x}^{6})^{6}}{18}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268957 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268958 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268959 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268960 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268961 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1041 "selection" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268961 13194139533960 true] [17592186268956 1110 #uuid "4f57bef0-f08a-512a-8737-1cecc5e6aa04" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268957 1034 "\\frac{(4+{x}^{6})^{6}}{3}+C" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533960 true] [17592186268957 1111 #uuid "5a8d4332-8dbf-5542-a0c0-82fa609bfc53" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268958 1034 "\\frac{(4+{x}^{6})^{6}}{2}+C" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533960 true] [17592186268958 1111 #uuid "c6b5d3eb-3155-5749-9696-bd907c5f7669" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268959 1034 "\\frac{(4+{x}^{6})^{6}}{6}+C" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533960 true] [17592186268959 1111 #uuid "97f26a1a-dbba-5ae4-abe4-fc47c8b881f0" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268960 1034 "2(4+{x}^{6})^{6}+C" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533960 true] [17592186268960 1111 #uuid "4a8e858a-7e8d-5fc6-aa40-2d8012351a68" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268961 1034 "\\frac{(4+{x}^{6})^{6}}{18}+C" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533960 true] [17592186268961 1111 #uuid "c6ae30d9-7cf0-5bbc-9cce-34b1f60a5d48" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268962 1017 #edb/ref 17592186268963 13194139533960 true] [17592186268962 1089 "q-113715" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268962 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533960 true] [17592186268962 1100 "Calculate $\\int 2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+10}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268962 1113 #uuid "c719d4ad-7c2f-5ad1-8b4c-4707dea196f0" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268962 1145 "In this case, the $2{x}^{2}$ that's outside the square root isn't quite the derivative of ${x}^{3}+10.$ But the derivative is $3{x}^{2},$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu={x}^{3}+10.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u=2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{{x}^{3}+10}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3/2}}{(\\frac{3}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {u}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{({x}^{3}+10)^{3}}}{9}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268964 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268965 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268966 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268967 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268968 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1041 "selection" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268967 13194139533960 true] [17592186268963 1110 #uuid "5dd20dcf-42f7-591b-9305-4cdb92b420f8" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268964 1034 "\\frac{3\\sqrt{({x}^{3}+10)^{3}}}{2}+C" 13194139533960 true] [17592186268964 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533960 true] [17592186268964 1111 #uuid "29e6e1af-f7f8-5e61-